commit 00abb7fa90df4339ec75fc6b478449bafb222cf8
Author: John Paul Soliva <soliva.johnpaul@icloud.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 06:53:21 2026 +0900

    Irodori-TTS: add v4.1 and v4.1-MF (MeanFlow) support (#284)
    
    * Irodori-TTS: decode v4 / v4.1-MF config fields
    
    Add flow_parameterization (meanflow), the pretrained text encoder fields
    (text_encoder_type/revision/config, pretrained_projector_*), the embedded
    ModernBERT config (flat or transformers>=5 nested RoPE thetas) and
    ref_max_seconds. ref_max_seconds stays nil when a config omits it, so v1-v3
    reference handling is unchanged; v3 configs decode exactly as before.
    
    Mirrors yoshphys's Python port in Blaizzy/mlx-audio (98a021d0, b3cb138f).
    
    * Irodori-TTS: add ModernBERT encoder for v4
    
    Swift port of mlx_audio irodori_tts/modernbert.py: bidirectional
    ModernBERT (global attention every 3rd layer, sliding window elsewhere,
    separate global/local RoPE thetas in rotate_half form, GeGLU MLP, bias-free
    float32-accumulating LayerNorm). Property names follow the checkpoint's
    pretrained_text_backbone.backbone.* keys after camelCase sanitizing.
    
    With Python's padded inputs the hidden states of the 25-layer
    modernbert-ja-310m backbone are bit-identical to the Python port.
    
    * Irodori-TTS: v4 text/caption projectors and MeanFlow conditioning in the DiT
    
    v4 replaces the scratch text and caption encoders with the shared
    pretrained ModernBERT backbone plus per-condition linear/residual_mlp
    projectors. MeanFlow checkpoints add delta_cond_module, an interval-length
    (t - r) embedding summed into the timestep conditioning; forwardWithConditions
    takes deltaT and rejects it for RF-velocity models, as upstream does.
    
    * Irodori-TTS: add MeanFlow sampler and upstream CFG gating
    
    irodoriSampleEulerMeanFlow: linear 1->0 schedule, one conditional forward
    per step with delta_t = t - t_next, no CFG (v4.1-MF, 4 steps).
    
    The CFG sampler now skips caption guidance when the caption mask is empty
    and lets caption guidance alone enable CFG (upstream a8e51b42). Both
    samplers accept pre-encoded conditions so the encoders run once per
    utterance, and an optional initial noise for parity testing.
    
    * Irodori-TTS: load and run v4.1 / v4.1-MF checkpoints
    
    - Load the tokenizer bundled under tokenizer/ (sanitized copy in Caches;
      the downloaded files are not modified) and download it with the model.
    - v4 uses the upstream text normaliser (keeps 。/、, folds .., NFKC,
      depth-aware bracket stripping); v1-v3 keep the existing normaliser.
    - v4 drops token padding before the encoder; padded keys were masked
      everywhere, so this only removes work.
    - Encode conditions once and share them between duration prediction and
      the sampler (v3 output is bit-identical).
    - The zero-reference placeholder spans one full speaker patch; with v4's
      speaker_patch_size 4 it previously patched to an empty sequence.
    - Strip the caption and mask an empty one (upstream a9754f4d, 0e846d23);
      for v3 this only changes an empty or whitespace-padded voice string.
    - Cap reference audio at ref_max_seconds when the config sets it.
    - Expose per-phase timings as lastTimings.
    
    Based on yoshphys's Python v4 / MeanFlow port in Blaizzy/mlx-audio
    (98a021d0, 0e846d23, a8e51b42, a9754f4d, ece79de8, b3cb138f).
    
    * Irodori-TTS: add v4 / MeanFlow unit tests
    
    Offline tests on tiny configurations, with goldens produced by the Python
    mlx-audio implementation: v4.1-MF and v3 config decoding, ModernBERT
    forward (key mask + sliding window), the MeanFlow sampler, the zero
    reference with speaker patch size 4, and the upstream normaliser.
    
    * Irodori-TTS: document v4.1 and v4.1-MF
    
    * Fix Irodori tokenizer cache races and portable parity tests
    
    * Normalize published Irodori tokenizer cache URLs
    
